A||||5||Nightwing||what are some good V6's to swap into my 84 ?||||1||
Z||000000||Nightwing||04-26-2000||11:58 AM||||I have a 1984 2m4 notch back with the 4cyl man.  What i am wondering .. what car engines out there swap in without to many mod's ??<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-26-2000||03:30 PM||||None||||reg||12
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||04-26-2000||03:40 PM||||If you had a V6, there would be less hassle, but these swap in with the easiest first:<BR>3.4l= no kit necessary, relocation of starter and a couple of very minor mods & different flywheel<BR>Quad 4= not sure but I think it isn't that hard (not my engine of choice though)<BR>3.8l= recquires kit but pretty muck bolts up with different flywheel (didn't do much research as I didn't go this route)<BR>3.8sc=(same as above)<BR>3.4 DOHC= decklid strut must be removed, possible relocation of battery, flywheel, etc. Tight fit, kit recommended<BR>V8/Northstar=kits necesary||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-26-2000||04:30 PM||||I have done several V6 swaps replacing the four. A good swap is a 3.4 pushrod engine. Does not require any major components other then new fule pump and new throttle cable. Everything else is a bolt on.(well Just about anything.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-26-2000||05:27 PM||||First you must tell why it's running a  "4cyl man" instead of a motor.   ??????||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||04-26-2000||09:38 PM||||The 2.8 V6 swap is going to be the easiest, at least if you can find a donor car to grab motor/tranny mounts, engine wiring harness, ECM for the V6, and probably several other things I can't think of right now. If you can gather up all the parts, this is a bolt in. Anything else requires modification, lots of bucks for kits and/or fabrication. The 3.4 swap is one of the easier, less expensive swaps. Installing a 3800 engine is quite a bit more costly, but they are a damn fine motor and probably worth it in the long run.||||reg||1
